  "prediction": "Contributing to Qiskit Metal\n============================\n\nThank you for your interest in contributing to Qiskit Metal! We welcome contributions from the community to help improve and expand the capabilities of Qiskit Metal. This guide provides information on how to get started, coding standards, and the contribution process.\n\nGetting Started\n---------------\n\n1. **Set Up Your Development Environment**\n\n   - Clone the Qiskit Metal repository from GitHub.\n   - Install the required dependencies. It is recommended to use a virtual environment.\n   - Follow the installation instructions in the main README to ensure Qiskit Metal runs correctly on your system.\n\n2. **Understand the Codebase**\n\n   Qiskit Metal is a framework for designing quantum devices. Familiarize yourself with the architecture and main components by reviewing the documentation and exploring the source code.\n\n3. **Choose an Issue or Feature**\n\n   - Browse the issue tracker for open issues labeled as \"good first issue\" or \"help wanted\".\n   - Alternatively, propose a new feature or improvement by opening a discussion or issue.\n\nCoding Standards\n----------------\n\nTo maintain code quality and consistency, please adhere to the following guidelines:\n\n- **Code Style:** Follow PEP 8 style conventions for Python code.\n- **Documentation:** Document your code thoroughly using docstrings and comments where appropriate.\n- **Testing:** Write unit tests for new features or bug fixes. Ensure all tests pass before submitting a pull request.\n- **Commit Messages:** Use clear and descriptive commit messages that explain the purpose of the change.\n\nContribution Process\n--------------------\n\n1. **Fork the Repository**\n\n   Create a personal fork of the Qiskit Metal repository on GitHub.\n\n2. **Create a Branch**\n\n   Create a new branch for your feature or bug fix. Use a descriptive branch name related to your work.\n\n3. **Make Changes**\n\n   Implement your changes following the coding standards.\n\n4. **Run Tests**\n\n   Run the test suite to verify that your changes do not break existing functionality.\n\n5. **Submit a Pull Request**\n\n   - Push your branch to your fork.\n   - Open a pull request against the main Qiskit Metal repository.\n   - Provide a clear description of your changes and reference any related issues.\n\n6. **Code Review**\n\n   The Qiskit Metal maintainers will review your pull request and may request changes or provide feedback.\n\n7. **Merge**\n\n   Once approved, your changes will be merged into the main codebase.\n\nCommunity and Support\n---------------------\n\nIf you have questions or need help, please join the Qiskit community forums or chat channels. We encourage open communication and collaboration.\n\nThank you for contributing to Qiskit Metal! Your efforts help advance quantum computing research and development.",
